<article id="post-25958" class="post-25958 post type-post status-publish format-standard sticky hentry category-freelancing">
		<header class="entry-header">
		<h1 class="entry-title"><a href="https://chrisssims.wordpress.com/2016/08/27/its-me-chris-sims/" rel="bookmark">Who is Chris&nbsp;Sims?</a></h1>					<div class="entry-meta small-part">
				<span class="posted-on"><i class="fa fa-clock-o space-left-right"></i><a href="https://chrisssims.wordpress.com/2016/08/27/its-me-chris-sims/" rel="bookmark"><time class="entry-date published" datetime="2016-08-27T14:53:14+02:00">August 27, 2016</time><time class="updated" datetime="2020-12-26T18:43:20+01:00">December 26, 2020</time></a></span><span class="byline"> <i class="fa fa-user space-left-right"></i><span class="author vcard"><a class="url fn n" href="https://chrisssims.wordpress.com/author/chrisssims/">Chris S. Sims</a></span></span>			</div><!-- .entry-meta -->
			</header><!-- .entry-header -->

			<div class="entry-content">
			<h3><img data-attachment-id="25913" data-permalink="https://chrisssims.wordpress.com/home/img_1018/" data-orig-file="https://chrisssims.wordpress.com/wp-content/uploads/2016/08/img_1018.jpg" data-orig-size="1080,1080" data-comments-opened="1" data-image-meta="{&quot;aperture&quot;:&quot;0&quot;,&quot;credit&quot;:&quot;&quot;,&quot;camera&quot;:&quot;&quot;,&quot;caption&quot;:&quot;&quot;,&quot;created_timestamp&quot;:&quot;0&quot;,&quot;copyright&quot;:&quot;&quot;,&quot;focal_length&quot;:&quot;0&quot;,&quot;iso&quot;:&quot;0&quot;,&quot;shutter_speed&quot;:&quot;0&quot;,&quot;title&quot;:&quot;&quot;,&quot;orientation&quot;:&quot;1&quot;}" data-image-title="IMG_1018" data-image-description="" data-image-caption="" data-large-file="https://chrisssims.wordpress.com/wp-content/uploads/2016/08/img_1018.jpg?w=809" class="wp-image-25913 alignright" src="https://chrisssims.wordpress.com/wp-content/uploads/2016/08/img_1018.jpg" alt="IMG_1018" width="267" height="267" srcset="https://chrisssims.wordpress.com/wp-content/uploads/2016/08/img_1018.jpg?w=267&amp;h=267 267w, https://chrisssims.wordpress.com/wp-content/uploads/2016/08/img_1018.jpg?w=534&amp;h=534 534w, https://chrisssims.wordpress.com/wp-content/uploads/2016/08/img_1018.jpg?w=150&amp;h=150 150w, https://chrisssims.wordpress.com/wp-content/uploads/2016/08/img_1018.jpg?w=300&amp;h=300 300w" sizes="(max-width: 267px) 100vw, 267px" /></h3>
<p><strong>I’m a game creator</strong> with decades of proven and award-winning skill in writing, narrative and game design, editing, and graphic art. I’m also a <span class="css-901oao css-16my406 r-1qd0xha r-ad9z0x r-bcqeeo r-qvutc0">human&#8230; being.</span></p>
<p><strong>Hire me.</strong> Learn about my career, publications, and rates on my <a href="https://chrisssims.wordpress.com/work/">Work</a> page.</p>
<p><strong>Talk to me.</strong> <a href="https://chrisssims.wordpress.com/contact-me/">Drop me a line</a> if you like. Mention or connect with me on <a href="http://twitter.com/ChrisSSims" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Twitter</a>.</p>
<p><strong>My blog starts just below.</strong></p>


<div class="wp-block-group is-layout-flow wp-block-group-is-layout-flow"><div class="wp-block-group__inner-container"></div></div>
		</div><!-- .entry-content -->
	
	<footer class="entry-footer">
		<div class="entry-bottom small-part">
					</div>
	</footer><!-- .entry-footer -->
</article><!-- #post-## -->
			
				
<article id="post-27790" class="post-27790 post type-post status-publish format-standard has-post-thumbnail hentry category-advice category-freelancing category-opinions category-roleplaying-games category-world-building category-writing">
				<figure class="entry-featured-image">
				<a href="https://chrisssims.wordpress.com/2020/07/14/writing-generalizations-and-absolutes/" rel="bookmark" title="Writing: Generalizations and&nbsp;Absolutes">
					<img width="768" height="445" src="https://chrisssims.wordpress.com/wp-content/uploads/2020/07/writingcollage-1.png?w=768" class="attachment-nucleare-normal-post size-nucleare-normal-post wp-post-image" alt="" decoding="async" srcset="https://chrisssims.wordpress.com/wp-content/uploads/2020/07/writingcollage-1.png 768w, https://chrisssims.wordpress.com/wp-content/uploads/2020/07/writingcollage-1.png?w=150 150w, https://chrisssims.wordpress.com/wp-content/uploads/2020/07/writingcollage-1.png?w=300 300w" sizes="(max-width: 768px) 100vw, 768px" data-attachment-id="27818" data-permalink="https://chrisssims.wordpress.com/2020/07/14/writing-generalizations-and-absolutes/writingcollage/" data-orig-file="https://chrisssims.wordpress.com/wp-content/uploads/2020/07/writingcollage-1.png" data-orig-size="768,445" data-comments-opened="1" data-image-meta="{&quot;aperture&quot;:&quot;0&quot;,&quot;credit&quot;:&quot;&quot;,&quot;camera&quot;:&quot;&quot;,&quot;caption&quot;:&quot;&quot;,&quot;created_timestamp&quot;:&quot;0&quot;,&quot;copyright&quot;:&quot;&quot;,&quot;focal_length&quot;:&quot;0&quot;,&quot;iso&quot;:&quot;0&quot;,&quot;shutter_speed&quot;:&quot;0&quot;,&quot;title&quot;:&quot;&quot;,&quot;orientation&quot;:&quot;0&quot;}" data-image-title="writingcollage" data-image-description="" data-image-caption="" data-large-file="https://chrisssims.wordpress.com/wp-content/uploads/2020/07/writingcollage-1.png?w=768" />					<figcaption><p><i class="fa fa-file-text"></i></p></figcaption>
				</a>
			</figure>
		<header class="entry-header">
		<h1 class="entry-title"><a href="https://chrisssims.wordpress.com/2020/07/14/writing-generalizations-and-absolutes/" rel="bookmark">Writing: Generalizations and&nbsp;Absolutes</a></h1>					<div class="entry-meta small-part">
				<span class="posted-on"><i class="fa fa-clock-o space-left-right"></i><a href="https://chrisssims.wordpress.com/2020/07/14/writing-generalizations-and-absolutes/" rel="bookmark"><time class="entry-date published updated" datetime="2020-07-14T18:38:40+02:00">July 14, 2020</time></a></span><span class="byline"> <i class="fa fa-user space-left-right"></i><span class="author vcard"><a class="url fn n" href="https://chrisssims.wordpress.com/author/chrisssims/">Chris S. Sims</a></span></span><span class="comments-link"><i class="fa fa-comments-o space-left-right"></i><a href="https://chrisssims.wordpress.com/2020/07/14/writing-generalizations-and-absolutes/#respond">Leave a comment</a></span>			</div><!-- .entry-meta -->
			</header><!-- .entry-header -->

			<div class="entry-content">
			<p>I have something to say about writing and game design re generalizations, hedging, and superlatives. <a href="#1">(1)</a> All three see common usage, but they’re hard to do well. I know. I’ve made all these mistakes at some point. I’m thankful I had mentors and colleagues to free me from these illusions. Among them is the great Kim Mohan, who probably attempted to teach me more than I could absorb.</p>
<p>As an editor and technical editor (also called <em>developer</em> in some places), I’ve seen misuse or overuse of generalizations, hedging, and superlatives a lot. Maybe rather than <em>mis-</em> or <em>over-</em>, the usage is more unintentional. I’ve also seen them in preproof passes, added during other phases of editing. Allow me to pay the help I had forward if you like.</p>
<p>This post doesn’t contain rules. Such prescription is folly. Everything is food for thought. If you take away one thing, I hope it’s conscientious usage. Writing is about choices—intention and refined intention. You’ll have your voice, and it’ll be different from any other. The context of your work matters, too—fiction is different from game descriptions or mechanics.<a class="more-link" href="https://chrisssims.wordpress.com/2020/07/14/writing-generalizations-and-absolutes/">Read More &raquo;</a></p>
<div id="atatags-370373-6a9e2a70cd34f">
		<script type="text/javascript">
			__ATA = window.__ATA || {};
			__ATA.cmd = window.__ATA.cmd || [];
			__ATA.cmd.push(function() {
				__ATA.initVideoSlot('atatags-370373-6a9e2a70cd34f', {
					sectionId: '370373',
					format: 'inread'
				});
			});
		</script>
	</div>
		</div><!-- .entry-content -->
	
	<footer class="entry-footer">
		<div class="entry-bottom small-part">
					</div>
	</footer><!-- .entry-footer -->
</article><!-- #post-## -->
			
				
<article id="post-27757" class="post-27757 post type-post status-publish format-standard has-post-thumbnail hentry category-movies category-opinions category-review category-science-fiction-fantasy category-world-building">
				<figure class="entry-featured-image">
				<a href="https://chrisssims.wordpress.com/2020/07/06/a-dim-view-of-bright/" rel="bookmark" title="Opinion: A Dim View of&nbsp;Bright">
					<img width="810" height="472" src="https://chrisssims.wordpress.com/wp-content/uploads/2020/07/bright.png?w=810" class="attachment-nucleare-normal-post size-nucleare-normal-post wp-post-image" alt="" decoding="async" srcset="https://chrisssims.wordpress.com/wp-content/uploads/2020/07/bright.png?w=810 810w, https://chrisssims.wordpress.com/wp-content/uploads/2020/07/bright.png?w=150 150w, https://chrisssims.wordpress.com/wp-content/uploads/2020/07/bright.png?w=300 300w, https://chrisssims.wordpress.com/wp-content/uploads/2020/07/bright.png?w=768 768w, https://chrisssims.wordpress.com/wp-content/uploads/2020/07/bright.png 963w" sizes="(max-width: 810px) 100vw, 810px" data-attachment-id="27764" data-permalink="https://chrisssims.wordpress.com/2020/07/06/a-dim-view-of-bright/bright/" data-orig-file="https://chrisssims.wordpress.com/wp-content/uploads/2020/07/bright.png" data-orig-size="963,561" data-comments-opened="1" data-image-meta="{&quot;aperture&quot;:&quot;0&quot;,&quot;credit&quot;:&quot;&quot;,&quot;camera&quot;:&quot;&quot;,&quot;caption&quot;:&quot;&quot;,&quot;created_timestamp&quot;:&quot;0&quot;,&quot;copyright&quot;:&quot;&quot;,&quot;focal_length&quot;:&quot;0&quot;,&quot;iso&quot;:&quot;0&quot;,&quot;shutter_speed&quot;:&quot;0&quot;,&quot;title&quot;:&quot;&quot;,&quot;orientation&quot;:&quot;0&quot;}" data-image-title="Bright" data-image-description="" data-image-caption="" data-large-file="https://chrisssims.wordpress.com/wp-content/uploads/2020/07/bright.png?w=809" />					<figcaption><p><i class="fa fa-file-text"></i></p></figcaption>
				</a>
			</figure>
		<header class="entry-header">
		<h1 class="entry-title"><a href="https://chrisssims.wordpress.com/2020/07/06/a-dim-view-of-bright/" rel="bookmark">Opinion: A Dim View of&nbsp;Bright</a></h1>					<div class="entry-meta small-part">
				<span class="posted-on"><i class="fa fa-clock-o space-left-right"></i><a href="https://chrisssims.wordpress.com/2020/07/06/a-dim-view-of-bright/" rel="bookmark"><time class="entry-date published" datetime="2020-07-06T14:19:27+02:00">July 6, 2020</time><time class="updated" datetime="2020-07-14T11:37:59+02:00">July 14, 2020</time></a></span><span class="byline"> <i class="fa fa-user space-left-right"></i><span class="author vcard"><a class="url fn n" href="https://chrisssims.wordpress.com/author/chrisssims/">Chris S. Sims</a></span></span><span class="comments-link"><i class="fa fa-comments-o space-left-right"></i><a href="https://chrisssims.wordpress.com/2020/07/06/a-dim-view-of-bright/#comments">3 Comments</a></span>			</div><!-- .entry-meta -->
			</header><!-- .entry-header -->

			<div class="entry-content">
			<p>This essay is something I don’t usually do, which is dunk on things I don’t like. I try to frame things in terms of why I do like them or what I want them to become. But I wrote this one as a supplement to my <a href="http://chrisssims.com/2020/07/01/world-building-imaginary-people/" target="_blank" rel="noopener">blog on imaginary people</a>. I did so not because this piece is at all timely, but because a good friend skilled in literary criticism, and a former colleague at Paizo, <a href="https://twitter.com/doctorcomics" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Jason Tondro</a> asked me why I’m on about <em>Bright</em> in that imaginary-people post. And listen, please, if you haven’t seen <em>Bright</em>, don’t bother. The <a href="https://www.rottentomatoes.com/m/bright" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Rotten Tomatoes consensus</a> says, “Bright tries to blend fantasy, hard-hitting cop drama, and social commentary—and ends up falling painfully short of the mark on all three fronts.” That’s generous.<br />
<a class="more-link" href="https://chrisssims.wordpress.com/2020/07/06/a-dim-view-of-bright/">Read More &raquo;</a></p>
		</div><!-- .entry-content -->
	
	<footer class="entry-footer">
		<div class="entry-bottom small-part">
					</div>
	</footer><!-- .entry-footer -->
</article><!-- #post-## -->
			
				
<article id="post-27675" class="post-27675 post type-post status-publish format-standard has-post-thumbnail hentry category-advice category-game-design category-game-mastering category-opinions category-roleplaying category-roleplaying-games category-science-fiction-fantasy category-setting category-world-building category-writing">
				<figure class="entry-featured-image">
				<a href="https://chrisssims.wordpress.com/2020/07/01/world-building-imaginary-people/" rel="bookmark" title="World Building: Imaginary&nbsp;People">
					<img width="672" height="393" src="https://chrisssims.wordpress.com/wp-content/uploads/2020/06/holger-link-r3zuzjjr59w-unsplash.png?w=672" class="attachment-nucleare-normal-post size-nucleare-normal-post wp-post-image" alt="" decoding="async" loading="lazy" srcset="https://chrisssims.wordpress.com/wp-content/uploads/2020/06/holger-link-r3zuzjjr59w-unsplash.png 672w, https://chrisssims.wordpress.com/wp-content/uploads/2020/06/holger-link-r3zuzjjr59w-unsplash.png?w=150 150w, https://chrisssims.wordpress.com/wp-content/uploads/2020/06/holger-link-r3zuzjjr59w-unsplash.png?w=300 300w" sizes="auto, (max-width: 672px) 100vw, 672px" data-attachment-id="27678" data-permalink="https://chrisssims.wordpress.com/2020/07/01/world-building-imaginary-people/holger-link-r3zuzjjr59w-unsplash/" data-orig-file="https://chrisssims.wordpress.com/wp-content/uploads/2020/06/holger-link-r3zuzjjr59w-unsplash.png" data-orig-size="672,393" data-comments-opened="1" data-image-meta="{&quot;aperture&quot;:&quot;0&quot;,&quot;credit&quot;:&quot;&quot;,&quot;camera&quot;:&quot;&quot;,&quot;caption&quot;:&quot;&quot;,&quot;created_timestamp&quot;:&quot;0&quot;,&quot;copyright&quot;:&quot;&quot;,&quot;focal_length&quot;:&quot;0&quot;,&quot;iso&quot;:&quot;0&quot;,&quot;shutter_speed&quot;:&quot;0&quot;,&quot;title&quot;:&quot;&quot;,&quot;orientation&quot;:&quot;0&quot;}" data-image-title="holger-link-r3ZUzJjR59w-unsplash" data-image-description="" data-image-caption="" data-large-file="https://chrisssims.wordpress.com/wp-content/uploads/2020/06/holger-link-r3zuzjjr59w-unsplash.png?w=672" />					<figcaption><p><i class="fa fa-file-text"></i></p></figcaption>
				</a>
			</figure>
		<header class="entry-header">
		<h1 class="entry-title"><a href="https://chrisssims.wordpress.com/2020/07/01/world-building-imaginary-people/" rel="bookmark">World Building: Imaginary&nbsp;People</a></h1>					<div class="entry-meta small-part">
				<span class="posted-on"><i class="fa fa-clock-o space-left-right"></i><a href="https://chrisssims.wordpress.com/2020/07/01/world-building-imaginary-people/" rel="bookmark"><time class="entry-date published" datetime="2020-07-01T18:24:56+02:00">July 1, 2020</time><time class="updated" datetime="2020-07-06T14:19:53+02:00">July 6, 2020</time></a></span><span class="byline"> <i class="fa fa-user space-left-right"></i><span class="author vcard"><a class="url fn n" href="https://chrisssims.wordpress.com/author/chrisssims/">Chris S. Sims</a></span></span><span class="comments-link"><i class="fa fa-comments-o space-left-right"></i><a href="https://chrisssims.wordpress.com/2020/07/01/world-building-imaginary-people/#comments">3 Comments</a></span>			</div><!-- .entry-meta -->
			</header><!-- .entry-header -->

			<div class="entry-content">
			<p>A furor among several old-guard D&amp;D creators prompted me to write this. Hyperbole, logical fallacies, and blinkered and outmoded thinking were on full display. Dismaying was the anti-progress and anti-sensitivity in evidence. So was the clear lack of understanding about modern gaming and games, including D&amp;D as it exists today. Unsophisticated was the understanding of how communication and other shared experiences, such as streaming, affect gaming today.</p>
<p>Worse was a hidebound adherence to an outdated way of thinking about how games depict imaginary people. To these veterans, evil must be absolute so the good might discern and righteously smite it. The point here is not to vilify these guys for their shallow takes. I disagree with them, though. I’ll go into why, starting with the topic of recent discourse.</p>
<p><a class="more-link" href="https://chrisssims.wordpress.com/2020/07/01/world-building-imaginary-people/">Read More &raquo;</a></p>
		</div><!-- .entry-content -->
	
	<footer class="entry-footer">
		<div class="entry-bottom small-part">
					</div>
	</footer><!-- .entry-footer -->
</article><!-- #post-## -->
			
				
<article id="post-27604" class="post-27604 post type-post status-publish format-standard has-post-thumbnail hentry category-advice category-game-mastering category-house-rules category-roleplaying category-roleplaying-games">
				<figure class="entry-featured-image">
				<a href="https://chrisssims.wordpress.com/2020/04/20/playing-advantage-and-inspiration-2/" rel="bookmark" title="Playing Advantage and Inspiration&nbsp;2">
					<img width="810" height="256" src="https://chrisssims.wordpress.com/wp-content/uploads/2020/04/knights.png?w=810" class="attachment-nucleare-normal-post size-nucleare-normal-post wp-post-image" alt="" decoding="async" loading="lazy" srcset="https://chrisssims.wordpress.com/wp-content/uploads/2020/04/knights.png?w=810 810w, https://chrisssims.wordpress.com/wp-content/uploads/2020/04/knights.png?w=150 150w, https://chrisssims.wordpress.com/wp-content/uploads/2020/04/knights.png?w=300 300w, https://chrisssims.wordpress.com/wp-content/uploads/2020/04/knights.png?w=768 768w, https://chrisssims.wordpress.com/wp-content/uploads/2020/04/knights.png 912w" sizes="auto, (max-width: 810px) 100vw, 810px" data-attachment-id="27608" data-permalink="https://chrisssims.wordpress.com/2020/04/20/playing-advantage-and-inspiration-2/knights/" data-orig-file="https://chrisssims.wordpress.com/wp-content/uploads/2020/04/knights.png" data-orig-size="912,288" data-comments-opened="1" data-image-meta="{&quot;aperture&quot;:&quot;0&quot;,&quot;credit&quot;:&quot;&quot;,&quot;camera&quot;:&quot;&quot;,&quot;caption&quot;:&quot;&quot;,&quot;created_timestamp&quot;:&quot;0&quot;,&quot;copyright&quot;:&quot;&quot;,&quot;focal_length&quot;:&quot;0&quot;,&quot;iso&quot;:&quot;0&quot;,&quot;shutter_speed&quot;:&quot;0&quot;,&quot;title&quot;:&quot;&quot;,&quot;orientation&quot;:&quot;0&quot;}" data-image-title="knights" data-image-description="" data-image-caption="" data-large-file="https://chrisssims.wordpress.com/wp-content/uploads/2020/04/knights.png?w=809" />					<figcaption><p><i class="fa fa-file-text"></i></p></figcaption>
				</a>
			</figure>
		<header class="entry-header">
		<h1 class="entry-title"><a href="https://chrisssims.wordpress.com/2020/04/20/playing-advantage-and-inspiration-2/" rel="bookmark">Playing Advantage and Inspiration&nbsp;2</a></h1>					<div class="entry-meta small-part">
				<span class="posted-on"><i class="fa fa-clock-o space-left-right"></i><a href="https://chrisssims.wordpress.com/2020/04/20/playing-advantage-and-inspiration-2/" rel="bookmark"><time class="entry-date published updated" datetime="2020-04-20T03:38:12+02:00">April 20, 2020</time></a></span><span class="byline"> <i class="fa fa-user space-left-right"></i><span class="author vcard"><a class="url fn n" href="https://chrisssims.wordpress.com/author/chrisssims/">Chris S. Sims</a></span></span><span class="comments-link"><i class="fa fa-comments-o space-left-right"></i><a href="https://chrisssims.wordpress.com/2020/04/20/playing-advantage-and-inspiration-2/#comments">1 Comment</a></span>			</div><!-- .entry-meta -->
			</header><!-- .entry-header -->

			<div class="entry-content">
			<p>The <a href="http://chrisssims.com/2020/04/11/playing-advantage-and-inspiration-1/" target="_blank" rel="noopener">last part</a> of this pair of posts spoke about changing advantage, disadvantage, and inspiration for D&amp;D. It suggested changing advantage to smaller add-on dice (d3s, d4s, d6s) that can stack. Using that alternative also allows for inspiration to accumulate rather than stagnate. An accumulation of inspiration dice allows for another mechanic to find its way into D&amp;D and other d20 games that incorporate this set of house rules. (And these advantage/disadvantage rules can be used to replace numeric modifiers in most d20 games.)<a class="more-link" href="https://chrisssims.wordpress.com/2020/04/20/playing-advantage-and-inspiration-2/">Read More &raquo;</a></p>
		</div><!-- .entry-content -->
	
	<footer class="entry-footer">
		<div class="entry-bottom small-part">
					</div>
	</footer><!-- .entry-footer -->
</article><!-- #post-## -->
			
				
<article id="post-27561" class="post-27561 post type-post status-publish format-standard has-post-thumbnail hentry category-advice category-game-design category-game-mastering category-house-rules category-opinions category-roleplaying-games">
				<figure class="entry-featured-image">
				<a href="https://chrisssims.wordpress.com/2020/04/11/playing-advantage-and-inspiration-1/" rel="bookmark" title="Playing Advantage and Inspiration&nbsp;1">
					<img width="774" height="480" src="https://chrisssims.wordpress.com/wp-content/uploads/2020/04/dice.png?w=774" class="attachment-nucleare-normal-post size-nucleare-normal-post wp-post-image" alt="" decoding="async" loading="lazy" srcset="https://chrisssims.wordpress.com/wp-content/uploads/2020/04/dice.png 774w, https://chrisssims.wordpress.com/wp-content/uploads/2020/04/dice.png?w=150 150w, https://chrisssims.wordpress.com/wp-content/uploads/2020/04/dice.png?w=300 300w, https://chrisssims.wordpress.com/wp-content/uploads/2020/04/dice.png?w=768 768w" sizes="auto, (max-width: 774px) 100vw, 774px" data-attachment-id="27564" data-permalink="https://chrisssims.wordpress.com/2020/04/11/playing-advantage-and-inspiration-1/dice-2/" data-orig-file="https://chrisssims.wordpress.com/wp-content/uploads/2020/04/dice.png" data-orig-size="774,480" data-comments-opened="1" data-image-meta="{&quot;aperture&quot;:&quot;0&quot;,&quot;credit&quot;:&quot;&quot;,&quot;camera&quot;:&quot;&quot;,&quot;caption&quot;:&quot;&quot;,&quot;created_timestamp&quot;:&quot;0&quot;,&quot;copyright&quot;:&quot;&quot;,&quot;focal_length&quot;:&quot;0&quot;,&quot;iso&quot;:&quot;0&quot;,&quot;shutter_speed&quot;:&quot;0&quot;,&quot;title&quot;:&quot;&quot;,&quot;orientation&quot;:&quot;0&quot;}" data-image-title="dice" data-image-description="" data-image-caption="" data-large-file="https://chrisssims.wordpress.com/wp-content/uploads/2020/04/dice.png?w=774" />					<figcaption><p><i class="fa fa-file-text"></i></p></figcaption>
				</a>
			</figure>
		<header class="entry-header">
		<h1 class="entry-title"><a href="https://chrisssims.wordpress.com/2020/04/11/playing-advantage-and-inspiration-1/" rel="bookmark">Playing Advantage and Inspiration&nbsp;1</a></h1>					<div class="entry-meta small-part">
				<span class="posted-on"><i class="fa fa-clock-o space-left-right"></i><a href="https://chrisssims.wordpress.com/2020/04/11/playing-advantage-and-inspiration-1/" rel="bookmark"><time class="entry-date published" datetime="2020-04-11T22:36:41+02:00">April 11, 2020</time><time class="updated" datetime="2020-04-20T03:39:32+02:00">April 20, 2020</time></a></span><span class="byline"> <i class="fa fa-user space-left-right"></i><span class="author vcard"><a class="url fn n" href="https://chrisssims.wordpress.com/author/chrisssims/">Chris S. Sims</a></span></span><span class="comments-link"><i class="fa fa-comments-o space-left-right"></i><a href="https://chrisssims.wordpress.com/2020/04/11/playing-advantage-and-inspiration-1/#comments">4 Comments</a></span>			</div><!-- .entry-meta -->
			</header><!-- .entry-header -->

			<div class="entry-content">
			<p>I have a love-hate relationship with D&amp;D’s advantage-disadvantage mechanics. And so, I have a similar relationship to inspiration. Inspiration is more tolerate-hate. With that opinion, I don’t blame groups for ignoring the decidedly uninspired inspiration rules. However, I’m not one to wax negative about something in a game without suggesting fixes I’d use. That’s what this piece is about.<a class="more-link" href="https://chrisssims.wordpress.com/2020/04/11/playing-advantage-and-inspiration-1/">Read More &raquo;</a></p>
		</div><!-- .entry-content -->
	
	<footer class="entry-footer">
		<div class="entry-bottom small-part">
					</div>
	</footer><!-- .entry-footer -->
</article><!-- #post-## -->
			
				
<article id="post-27487" class="post-27487 post type-post status-publish format-standard has-post-thumbnail hentry category-advice category-game-mastering category-house-rules category-opinions category-roleplaying category-roleplaying-games">
				<figure class="entry-featured-image">
				<a href="https://chrisssims.wordpress.com/2020/03/30/playing-with-passive-expertise-3/" rel="bookmark" title="Playing with Passive Expertise&nbsp;3">
					<img width="810" height="456" src="https://chrisssims.wordpress.com/wp-content/uploads/2020/03/levels.png?w=810" class="attachment-nucleare-normal-post size-nucleare-normal-post wp-post-image" alt="" decoding="async" loading="lazy" srcset="https://chrisssims.wordpress.com/wp-content/uploads/2020/03/levels.png?w=810 810w, https://chrisssims.wordpress.com/wp-content/uploads/2020/03/levels.png?w=150 150w, https://chrisssims.wordpress.com/wp-content/uploads/2020/03/levels.png?w=300 300w, https://chrisssims.wordpress.com/wp-content/uploads/2020/03/levels.png?w=768 768w, https://chrisssims.wordpress.com/wp-content/uploads/2020/03/levels.png 853w" sizes="auto, (max-width: 810px) 100vw, 810px" data-attachment-id="27494" data-permalink="https://chrisssims.wordpress.com/2020/03/30/playing-with-passive-expertise-3/levels/" data-orig-file="https://chrisssims.wordpress.com/wp-content/uploads/2020/03/levels.png" data-orig-size="853,480" data-comments-opened="1" data-image-meta="{&quot;aperture&quot;:&quot;0&quot;,&quot;credit&quot;:&quot;&quot;,&quot;camera&quot;:&quot;&quot;,&quot;caption&quot;:&quot;&quot;,&quot;created_timestamp&quot;:&quot;0&quot;,&quot;copyright&quot;:&quot;&quot;,&quot;focal_length&quot;:&quot;0&quot;,&quot;iso&quot;:&quot;0&quot;,&quot;shutter_speed&quot;:&quot;0&quot;,&quot;title&quot;:&quot;&quot;,&quot;orientation&quot;:&quot;0&quot;}" data-image-title="levels" data-image-description="" data-image-caption="" data-large-file="https://chrisssims.wordpress.com/wp-content/uploads/2020/03/levels.png?w=809" />					<figcaption><p><i class="fa fa-file-text"></i></p></figcaption>
				</a>
			</figure>
		<header class="entry-header">
		<h1 class="entry-title"><a href="https://chrisssims.wordpress.com/2020/03/30/playing-with-passive-expertise-3/" rel="bookmark">Playing with Passive Expertise&nbsp;3</a></h1>					<div class="entry-meta small-part">
				<span class="posted-on"><i class="fa fa-clock-o space-left-right"></i><a href="https://chrisssims.wordpress.com/2020/03/30/playing-with-passive-expertise-3/" rel="bookmark"><time class="entry-date published" datetime="2020-03-30T03:31:54+02:00">March 30, 2020</time><time class="updated" datetime="2020-05-03T02:37:24+02:00">May 3, 2020</time></a></span><span class="byline"> <i class="fa fa-user space-left-right"></i><span class="author vcard"><a class="url fn n" href="https://chrisssims.wordpress.com/author/chrisssims/">Chris S. Sims</a></span></span><span class="comments-link"><i class="fa fa-comments-o space-left-right"></i><a href="https://chrisssims.wordpress.com/2020/03/30/playing-with-passive-expertise-3/#comments">1 Comment</a></span>			</div><!-- .entry-meta -->
			</header><!-- .entry-header -->

			<div class="entry-content">
			<p>This series has been about allowing characters to be awesome based on what’s on display on the character sheet. In <a href="http://chrisssims.com/2020/02/13/playing-passive-expertise-1/">part 1</a>, I talk about using the characters’ passive expertise as an excuse to give players the information they need. The wizard is good at knowing magical and occult facts. Give those facts to the wizard’s player. <a href="http://chrisssims.com/2020/03/01/playing-with-passive-expertise-2/">Part 2</a> is about allowing a character to pull off amazing stunts based on physical skills they have. Great at acrobatics? Then, as we see in action movies, you can run up a wall and backflip. No problem. In both cases, the point is to do allow a lot of this stuff to happen without rolls.</p>
<p>This part deviates from that theory. Some people like to roll; it’s a game. That’s valid. But you can have your rolls and emphasize expertise, too. I’ll go into a few options.<a class="more-link" href="https://chrisssims.wordpress.com/2020/03/30/playing-with-passive-expertise-3/">Read More &raquo;</a></p>
		</div><!-- .entry-content -->
	
	<footer class="entry-footer">
		<div class="entry-bottom small-part">
					</div>
	</footer><!-- .entry-footer -->
</article><!-- #post-## -->
			
				
<article id="post-27424" class="post-27424 post type-post status-publish format-standard has-post-thumbnail hentry category-advice category-game-mastering category-house-rules category-opinions category-roleplaying category-roleplaying-games">
				<figure class="entry-featured-image">
				<a href="https://chrisssims.wordpress.com/2020/03/01/playing-with-passive-expertise-2/" rel="bookmark" title="Playing with Passive Expertise&nbsp;2">
					<img width="810" height="424" src="https://chrisssims.wordpress.com/wp-content/uploads/2020/03/acrobat-sunsetactive-adventure-1.jpg?w=810" class="attachment-nucleare-normal-post size-nucleare-normal-post wp-post-image" alt="" decoding="async" loading="lazy" srcset="https://chrisssims.wordpress.com/wp-content/uploads/2020/03/acrobat-sunsetactive-adventure-1.jpg?w=810 810w, https://chrisssims.wordpress.com/wp-content/uploads/2020/03/acrobat-sunsetactive-adventure-1.jpg?w=1620 1620w, https://chrisssims.wordpress.com/wp-content/uploads/2020/03/acrobat-sunsetactive-adventure-1.jpg?w=150 150w, https://chrisssims.wordpress.com/wp-content/uploads/2020/03/acrobat-sunsetactive-adventure-1.jpg?w=300 300w, https://chrisssims.wordpress.com/wp-content/uploads/2020/03/acrobat-sunsetactive-adventure-1.jpg?w=768 768w, https://chrisssims.wordpress.com/wp-content/uploads/2020/03/acrobat-sunsetactive-adventure-1.jpg?w=1024 1024w, https://chrisssims.wordpress.com/wp-content/uploads/2020/03/acrobat-sunsetactive-adventure-1.jpg?w=1440 1440w" sizes="auto, (max-width: 810px) 100vw, 810px" data-attachment-id="27443" data-permalink="https://chrisssims.wordpress.com/2020/03/01/playing-with-passive-expertise-2/acrobat-sunsetactive-adventure/" data-orig-file="https://chrisssims.wordpress.com/wp-content/uploads/2020/03/acrobat-sunsetactive-adventure-1.jpg" data-orig-size="1920,1005" data-comments-opened="1" data-image-meta="{&quot;aperture&quot;:&quot;0&quot;,&quot;credit&quot;:&quot;&quot;,&quot;camera&quot;:&quot;&quot;,&quot;caption&quot;:&quot;&quot;,&quot;created_timestamp&quot;:&quot;0&quot;,&quot;copyright&quot;:&quot;&quot;,&quot;focal_length&quot;:&quot;0&quot;,&quot;iso&quot;:&quot;0&quot;,&quot;shutter_speed&quot;:&quot;0&quot;,&quot;title&quot;:&quot;&quot;,&quot;orientation&quot;:&quot;0&quot;}" data-image-title="acrobat-sunsetactive-adventure" data-image-description="" data-image-caption="" data-large-file="https://chrisssims.wordpress.com/wp-content/uploads/2020/03/acrobat-sunsetactive-adventure-1.jpg?w=809" />					<figcaption><p><i class="fa fa-file-text"></i></p></figcaption>
				</a>
			</figure>
		<header class="entry-header">
		<h1 class="entry-title"><a href="https://chrisssims.wordpress.com/2020/03/01/playing-with-passive-expertise-2/" rel="bookmark">Playing with Passive Expertise&nbsp;2</a></h1>					<div class="entry-meta small-part">
				<span class="posted-on"><i class="fa fa-clock-o space-left-right"></i><a href="https://chrisssims.wordpress.com/2020/03/01/playing-with-passive-expertise-2/" rel="bookmark"><time class="entry-date published" datetime="2020-03-01T15:45:53+01:00">March 1, 2020</time><time class="updated" datetime="2020-03-30T03:38:46+02:00">March 30, 2020</time></a></span><span class="byline"> <i class="fa fa-user space-left-right"></i><span class="author vcard"><a class="url fn n" href="https://chrisssims.wordpress.com/author/chrisssims/">Chris S. Sims</a></span></span><span class="comments-link"><i class="fa fa-comments-o space-left-right"></i><a href="https://chrisssims.wordpress.com/2020/03/01/playing-with-passive-expertise-2/#comments">5 Comments</a></span>			</div><!-- .entry-meta -->
			</header><!-- .entry-header -->

			<div class="entry-content">
			<p>In the <a href="http://chrisssims.com/2020/02/13/playing-passive-expertise-1/" target="_blank" rel="noopener">first entry of this short series</a>, I wrote about the philosophy of passive skill or trait use in roleplaying games. That piece focused on information exchange and the use of passive skill to determine the baseline of what a character knows in a game. There, I claimed you could use passive skill, or almost any trait you might normally roll for, in active situations in a game.</p>
<p>What that claim means, in practical terms, is allowing player characters to have a bottom performance level in physical activities, such as athletics and stealth. This passive us fits alongside the mental acuity I advocated for in the first essay. For the sake of narration and speed of play, it’s fair for this floor of expertise to apply to NPCs, too. They can sometimes perform fancy maneuvers based on their capabilities just like the player characters.<a class="more-link" href="https://chrisssims.wordpress.com/2020/03/01/playing-with-passive-expertise-2/">Read More &raquo;</a></p>
		</div><!-- .entry-content -->
	
	<footer class="entry-footer">
		<div class="entry-bottom small-part">
					</div>
	</footer><!-- .entry-footer -->
</article><!-- #post-## -->
			
				
<article id="post-27382" class="post-27382 post type-post status-publish format-standard has-post-thumbnail hentry category-art category-game-design category-roleplaying category-roleplaying-games">
				<figure class="entry-featured-image">
				<a href="https://chrisssims.wordpress.com/2020/02/20/draculola-characters/" rel="bookmark" title="Playing Draculola Characters">
					<img width="810" height="427" src="https://chrisssims.wordpress.com/wp-content/uploads/2020/02/draculolalayered.png?w=810" class="attachment-nucleare-normal-post size-nucleare-normal-post wp-post-image" alt="" decoding="async" loading="lazy" srcset="https://chrisssims.wordpress.com/wp-content/uploads/2020/02/draculolalayered.png?w=810 810w, https://chrisssims.wordpress.com/wp-content/uploads/2020/02/draculolalayered.png?w=150 150w, https://chrisssims.wordpress.com/wp-content/uploads/2020/02/draculolalayered.png?w=300 300w, https://chrisssims.wordpress.com/wp-content/uploads/2020/02/draculolalayered.png?w=768 768w, https://chrisssims.wordpress.com/wp-content/uploads/2020/02/draculolalayered.png 846w" sizes="auto, (max-width: 810px) 100vw, 810px" data-attachment-id="27385" data-permalink="https://chrisssims.wordpress.com/2020/02/20/draculola-characters/draculolalayered/" data-orig-file="https://chrisssims.wordpress.com/wp-content/uploads/2020/02/draculolalayered.png" data-orig-size="846,446" data-comments-opened="1" data-image-meta="{&quot;aperture&quot;:&quot;0&quot;,&quot;credit&quot;:&quot;&quot;,&quot;camera&quot;:&quot;&quot;,&quot;caption&quot;:&quot;&quot;,&quot;created_timestamp&quot;:&quot;0&quot;,&quot;copyright&quot;:&quot;&quot;,&quot;focal_length&quot;:&quot;0&quot;,&quot;iso&quot;:&quot;0&quot;,&quot;shutter_speed&quot;:&quot;0&quot;,&quot;title&quot;:&quot;&quot;,&quot;orientation&quot;:&quot;0&quot;}" data-image-title="draculolalayered" data-image-description="" data-image-caption="" data-large-file="https://chrisssims.wordpress.com/wp-content/uploads/2020/02/draculolalayered.png?w=809" />					<figcaption><p><i class="fa fa-file-text"></i></p></figcaption>
				</a>
			</figure>
		<header class="entry-header">
		<h1 class="entry-title"><a href="https://chrisssims.wordpress.com/2020/02/20/draculola-characters/" rel="bookmark">Playing Draculola Characters</a></h1>					<div class="entry-meta small-part">
				<span class="posted-on"><i class="fa fa-clock-o space-left-right"></i><a href="https://chrisssims.wordpress.com/2020/02/20/draculola-characters/" rel="bookmark"><time class="entry-date published" datetime="2020-02-20T14:34:39+01:00">February 20, 2020</time><time class="updated" datetime="2020-03-30T03:41:01+02:00">March 30, 2020</time></a></span><span class="byline"> <i class="fa fa-user space-left-right"></i><span class="author vcard"><a class="url fn n" href="https://chrisssims.wordpress.com/author/chrisssims/">Chris S. Sims</a></span></span><span class="comments-link"><i class="fa fa-comments-o space-left-right"></i><a href="https://chrisssims.wordpress.com/2020/02/20/draculola-characters/#respond">Leave a comment</a></span>			</div><!-- .entry-meta -->
			</header><!-- .entry-header -->

			<div class="entry-content">
			<p>This post is a preview of the <em>Draculola</em> game rules for making characters. <a href="https://www.kickstarter.com/projects/chrisssims/draculola-roleplaying-game-zine-quest-2" target="_blank" rel="noopener">The game is on Kickstarter, and this link takes you there.</a> You can use the following section to make a character concept. (Characters by Rosie and Meri Sims, art by Emma Welch.)</p>
<p><strong>If you’re not the Narrator of the <em>Draculola</em> game, you need a character.</strong> Use guidelines here to make one.</p>
<p>This section often refers to your character as “you.” The players form a friendly group of characters that have differing qualities, so they work well together during play.<a class="more-link" href="https://chrisssims.wordpress.com/2020/02/20/draculola-characters/">Read More &raquo;</a></p>
		</div><!-- .entry-content -->
	
	<footer class="entry-footer">
		<div class="entry-bottom small-part">
					</div>
	</footer><!-- .entry-footer -->
</article><!-- #post-## -->
			
				
<article id="post-27352" class="post-27352 post type-post status-publish format-standard has-post-thumbnail hentry category-advice category-game-mastering category-house-rules category-opinions category-roleplaying category-roleplaying-games">
				<figure class="entry-featured-image">
				<a href="https://chrisssims.wordpress.com/2020/02/13/playing-passive-expertise-1/" rel="bookmark" title="Playing with Passive Expertise&nbsp;1">
					<img width="810" height="505" src="https://chrisssims.wordpress.com/wp-content/uploads/2020/02/walhall_by_emil_doepler.png?w=810" class="attachment-nucleare-normal-post size-nucleare-normal-post wp-post-image" alt="" decoding="async" loading="lazy" srcset="https://chrisssims.wordpress.com/wp-content/uploads/2020/02/walhall_by_emil_doepler.png?w=810 810w, https://chrisssims.wordpress.com/wp-content/uploads/2020/02/walhall_by_emil_doepler.png?w=150 150w, https://chrisssims.wordpress.com/wp-content/uploads/2020/02/walhall_by_emil_doepler.png?w=300 300w, https://chrisssims.wordpress.com/wp-content/uploads/2020/02/walhall_by_emil_doepler.png?w=768 768w, https://chrisssims.wordpress.com/wp-content/uploads/2020/02/walhall_by_emil_doepler.png?w=1024 1024w, https://chrisssims.wordpress.com/wp-content/uploads/2020/02/walhall_by_emil_doepler.png?w=1440 1440w, https://chrisssims.wordpress.com/wp-content/uploads/2020/02/walhall_by_emil_doepler.png 1530w" sizes="auto, (max-width: 810px) 100vw, 810px" data-attachment-id="27355" data-permalink="https://chrisssims.wordpress.com/2020/02/13/playing-passive-expertise-1/walhall_by_emil_doepler/" data-orig-file="https://chrisssims.wordpress.com/wp-content/uploads/2020/02/walhall_by_emil_doepler.png" data-orig-size="1530,953" data-comments-opened="1" data-image-meta="{&quot;aperture&quot;:&quot;0&quot;,&quot;credit&quot;:&quot;&quot;,&quot;camera&quot;:&quot;&quot;,&quot;caption&quot;:&quot;&quot;,&quot;created_timestamp&quot;:&quot;0&quot;,&quot;copyright&quot;:&quot;&quot;,&quot;focal_length&quot;:&quot;0&quot;,&quot;iso&quot;:&quot;0&quot;,&quot;shutter_speed&quot;:&quot;0&quot;,&quot;title&quot;:&quot;&quot;,&quot;orientation&quot;:&quot;0&quot;}" data-image-title="Walhall_by_Emil_Doepler" data-image-description="" data-image-caption="" data-large-file="https://chrisssims.wordpress.com/wp-content/uploads/2020/02/walhall_by_emil_doepler.png?w=809" />					<figcaption><p><i class="fa fa-file-text"></i></p></figcaption>
				</a>
			</figure>
		<header class="entry-header">
		<h1 class="entry-title"><a href="https://chrisssims.wordpress.com/2020/02/13/playing-passive-expertise-1/" rel="bookmark">Playing with Passive Expertise&nbsp;1</a></h1>					<div class="entry-meta small-part">
				<span class="posted-on"><i class="fa fa-clock-o space-left-right"></i><a href="https://chrisssims.wordpress.com/2020/02/13/playing-passive-expertise-1/" rel="bookmark"><time class="entry-date published" datetime="2020-02-13T18:17:24+01:00">February 13, 2020</time><time class="updated" datetime="2020-03-02T11:24:30+01:00">March 2, 2020</time></a></span><span class="byline"> <i class="fa fa-user space-left-right"></i><span class="author vcard"><a class="url fn n" href="https://chrisssims.wordpress.com/author/chrisssims/">Chris S. Sims</a></span></span><span class="comments-link"><i class="fa fa-comments-o space-left-right"></i><a href="https://chrisssims.wordpress.com/2020/02/13/playing-passive-expertise-1/#comments">4 Comments</a></span>			</div><!-- .entry-meta -->
			</header><!-- .entry-header -->

			<div class="entry-content">
			<p>In several tabletop roleplaying games, especially D&amp;D and its derivatives, we ask to roll too much as players. As referees, we ask for rolls too often, including confirming the player’s request to roll. Published adventures and rules call for rolling more than they should. It’s as if we think that rolling is essential whenever a question of success arises.</p>
<p>It isn’t.</p>
<p>Rolling a check is important only when stress is a factor, failure has consequences, or the feat of brains or brawn is possibly beyond those attempting it. Even in these cases, rolling isn’t vital. In some cases, it’s problematic for play.<a class="more-link" href="https://chrisssims.wordpress.com/2020/02/13/playing-passive-expertise-1/">Read More &raquo;</a></p>
		</div><!-- .entry-content -->
	
	<footer class="entry-footer">
		<div class="entry-bottom small-part">
					</div>
	</footer><!-- .entry-footer -->
</article><!-- #post-## -->
			
				
<article id="post-27253" class="post-27253 post type-post status-publish format-standard has-post-thumbnail hentry category-advice category-game-design category-game-mastering category-games category-house-rules category-opinions category-roleplaying category-roleplaying-games">
				<figure class="entry-featured-image">
				<a href="https://chrisssims.wordpress.com/2020/01/28/playing-in-imagination-space/" rel="bookmark" title="Playing in Imagination&nbsp;Space">
					<img width="810" height="369" src="https://chrisssims.wordpress.com/wp-content/uploads/2020/01/fractal.png?w=810" class="attachment-nucleare-normal-post size-nucleare-normal-post wp-post-image" alt="" decoding="async" loading="lazy" srcset="https://chrisssims.wordpress.com/wp-content/uploads/2020/01/fractal.png?w=810 810w, https://chrisssims.wordpress.com/wp-content/uploads/2020/01/fractal.png?w=150 150w, https://chrisssims.wordpress.com/wp-content/uploads/2020/01/fractal.png?w=300 300w, https://chrisssims.wordpress.com/wp-content/uploads/2020/01/fractal.png?w=768 768w, https://chrisssims.wordpress.com/wp-content/uploads/2020/01/fractal.png?w=1024 1024w, https://chrisssims.wordpress.com/wp-content/uploads/2020/01/fractal.png 1344w" sizes="auto, (max-width: 810px) 100vw, 810px" data-attachment-id="27257" data-permalink="https://chrisssims.wordpress.com/2020/01/28/playing-in-imagination-space/fractal/" data-orig-file="https://chrisssims.wordpress.com/wp-content/uploads/2020/01/fractal.png" data-orig-size="1344,613" data-comments-opened="1" data-image-meta="{&quot;aperture&quot;:&quot;0&quot;,&quot;credit&quot;:&quot;&quot;,&quot;camera&quot;:&quot;&quot;,&quot;caption&quot;:&quot;&quot;,&quot;created_timestamp&quot;:&quot;0&quot;,&quot;copyright&quot;:&quot;&quot;,&quot;focal_length&quot;:&quot;0&quot;,&quot;iso&quot;:&quot;0&quot;,&quot;shutter_speed&quot;:&quot;0&quot;,&quot;title&quot;:&quot;&quot;,&quot;orientation&quot;:&quot;0&quot;}" data-image-title="fractal" data-image-description="" data-image-caption="" data-large-file="https://chrisssims.wordpress.com/wp-content/uploads/2020/01/fractal.png?w=809" />					<figcaption><p><i class="fa fa-file-text"></i></p></figcaption>
				</a>
			</figure>
		<header class="entry-header">
		<h1 class="entry-title"><a href="https://chrisssims.wordpress.com/2020/01/28/playing-in-imagination-space/" rel="bookmark">Playing in Imagination&nbsp;Space</a></h1>					<div class="entry-meta small-part">
				<span class="posted-on"><i class="fa fa-clock-o space-left-right"></i><a href="https://chrisssims.wordpress.com/2020/01/28/playing-in-imagination-space/" rel="bookmark"><time class="entry-date published updated" datetime="2020-01-28T16:02:44+01:00">January 28, 2020</time></a></span><span class="byline"> <i class="fa fa-user space-left-right"></i><span class="author vcard"><a class="url fn n" href="https://chrisssims.wordpress.com/author/chrisssims/">Chris S. Sims</a></span></span><span class="comments-link"><i class="fa fa-comments-o space-left-right"></i><a href="https://chrisssims.wordpress.com/2020/01/28/playing-in-imagination-space/#respond">Leave a comment</a></span>			</div><!-- .entry-meta -->
			</header><!-- .entry-header -->

			<div class="entry-content">
			<p>When we were little kids, we roleplayed with few boundaries. The floor is lava! You avoid it, or you “die.” It was the same with playing adventurers versus monsters or space wizards with laser swords in the back yard after interacting with popular media, such as <em><a href="https://amzn.to/37zIZo1" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Dungeons &amp; Dragons</a></em> or <em>Star Wars</em>.</p>
<p>We didn’t have written rules. The parameters were contextual and freeform. Any rules that existed were negotiated, often on the spot. The imagination space was broad.</p>
<p>Imagination space is an ephemeral realm where creativity has free reign within parameters a game defines.<a class="more-link" href="https://chrisssims.wordpress.com/2020/01/28/playing-in-imagination-space/">Read More &raquo;</a></p>
		</div><!-- .entry-content -->
	
	<footer class="entry-footer">
		<div class="entry-bottom small-part">
					</div>
	</footer><!-- .entry-footer -->
</article><!-- #post-## -->
			
				
<article id="post-27112" class="post-27112 post type-post status-publish format-standard has-post-thumbnail hentry category-game-design category-roleplaying-games category-science-fiction-fantasy category-setting category-video-games category-world-building category-writing">
				<figure class="entry-featured-image">
				<a href="https://chrisssims.wordpress.com/2020/01/21/explain-a-game/" rel="bookmark" title="World Building: Explain a&nbsp;Game">
					<img width="800" height="481" src="https://chrisssims.wordpress.com/wp-content/uploads/2020/01/walter_crane_britomart.png?w=800" class="attachment-nucleare-normal-post size-nucleare-normal-post wp-post-image" alt="" decoding="async" loading="lazy" srcset="https://chrisssims.wordpress.com/wp-content/uploads/2020/01/walter_crane_britomart.png 800w, https://chrisssims.wordpress.com/wp-content/uploads/2020/01/walter_crane_britomart.png?w=150 150w, https://chrisssims.wordpress.com/wp-content/uploads/2020/01/walter_crane_britomart.png?w=300 300w, https://chrisssims.wordpress.com/wp-content/uploads/2020/01/walter_crane_britomart.png?w=768 768w" sizes="auto, (max-width: 800px) 100vw, 800px" data-attachment-id="27131" data-permalink="https://chrisssims.wordpress.com/2020/01/21/explain-a-game/walter_crane_britomart/" data-orig-file="https://chrisssims.wordpress.com/wp-content/uploads/2020/01/walter_crane_britomart.png" data-orig-size="800,481" data-comments-opened="1" data-image-meta="{&quot;aperture&quot;:&quot;0&quot;,&quot;credit&quot;:&quot;&quot;,&quot;camera&quot;:&quot;&quot;,&quot;caption&quot;:&quot;&quot;,&quot;created_timestamp&quot;:&quot;0&quot;,&quot;copyright&quot;:&quot;&quot;,&quot;focal_length&quot;:&quot;0&quot;,&quot;iso&quot;:&quot;0&quot;,&quot;shutter_speed&quot;:&quot;0&quot;,&quot;title&quot;:&quot;&quot;,&quot;orientation&quot;:&quot;0&quot;}" data-image-title="Walter_Crane_Britomart" data-image-description="" data-image-caption="" data-large-file="https://chrisssims.wordpress.com/wp-content/uploads/2020/01/walter_crane_britomart.png?w=800" />					<figcaption><p><i class="fa fa-file-text"></i></p></figcaption>
				</a>
			</figure>
		<header class="entry-header">
		<h1 class="entry-title"><a href="https://chrisssims.wordpress.com/2020/01/21/explain-a-game/" rel="bookmark">World Building: Explain a&nbsp;Game</a></h1>					<div class="entry-meta small-part">
				<span class="posted-on"><i class="fa fa-clock-o space-left-right"></i><a href="https://chrisssims.wordpress.com/2020/01/21/explain-a-game/" rel="bookmark"><time class="entry-date published" datetime="2020-01-21T11:39:49+01:00">January 21, 2020</time><time class="updated" datetime="2020-01-23T12:56:18+01:00">January 23, 2020</time></a></span><span class="byline"> <i class="fa fa-user space-left-right"></i><span class="author vcard"><a class="url fn n" href="https://chrisssims.wordpress.com/author/chrisssims/">Chris S. Sims</a></span></span><span class="comments-link"><i class="fa fa-comments-o space-left-right"></i><a href="https://chrisssims.wordpress.com/2020/01/21/explain-a-game/#respond">Leave a comment</a></span>			</div><!-- .entry-meta -->
			</header><!-- .entry-header -->

			<div class="entry-content">
			<p>Writing prompts can help you stretch your world-building and narrative skills, such as character development and story development. My friend, game designer and writer Owen K.C. Stephens regularly seeds such prompts on his <a href="https://twitter.com/Owen_Stephens" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Twitter feed</a>. Several products on the market, from the <a href="https://www.kickstarter.com/projects/rockpapercynic/the-story-engine-deck-of-endless-storytelling-prompts-book/description" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Story Engine</a> to the <a href="https://amzn.to/2uaKUAH" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Writer Emergency Pack</a>, aim at feeding prompts or breaking blocks. Writing as an exercise can be fun and creative, as well as training.</p>
<p>In that vein, Ryan Kaufman, a veteran of story who has worked at LucasArts and Telltale, gave out random prompts on request. These prompts were from a narrative-design exercise he did with his writers at Jam City, where he’s VP of Narrative. This is how it started (click the date to see the thread).</p>
<blockquote>
<p dir="ltr" lang="en">I&#8217;m running a narrative design exercise with the Jam City writers where we are randomly assigned a Character Backstory, a Goal, and a Game Genre. Then, we will attempt to explain the resulting game, and how all these things fit together as a ridiculous whole.</p>
<p>— Ryan Kaufman (@M1sterFox) <a href="https://twitter.com/M1sterFox/status/1196633859305009152?ref_src=twsrc%5Etfw">November 19, 2019</a></p></blockquote>
<p>If you asked Ryan, you received a random character, goal, and game type. Then you explain that game. I asked for a prompt and got the following. <a href="#1">(1)</a></p>
<p><strong>An unusually tall young woman wants to win the Wimbledon in a hack-and-slash.<br />
</strong><a class="more-link" href="https://chrisssims.wordpress.com/2020/01/21/explain-a-game/">Read More &raquo;</a></p>
		</div><!-- .entry-content -->
	
	<footer class="entry-footer">
		<div class="entry-bottom small-part">
					</div>
	</footer><!-- .entry-footer -->
</article><!-- #post-## -->
			
				
<article id="post-27003" class="post-27003 post type-post status-publish format-standard has-post-thumbnail hentry category-advice category-game-design category-game-mastering category-house-rules category-opinions category-roleplaying category-roleplaying-games category-world-building">
				<figure class="entry-featured-image">
				<a href="https://chrisssims.wordpress.com/2020/01/12/exceptional-scores/" rel="bookmark" title="Playing with Exceptional&nbsp;Scores">
					<img width="810" height="318" src="https://chrisssims.wordpress.com/wp-content/uploads/2020/01/scores.png?w=810" class="attachment-nucleare-normal-post size-nucleare-normal-post wp-post-image" alt="The Fall of the Rebel Angels by Pieter Bruegel the Elder (1562)." decoding="async" loading="lazy" srcset="https://chrisssims.wordpress.com/wp-content/uploads/2020/01/scores.png?w=810 810w, https://chrisssims.wordpress.com/wp-content/uploads/2020/01/scores.png?w=150 150w, https://chrisssims.wordpress.com/wp-content/uploads/2020/01/scores.png?w=300 300w, https://chrisssims.wordpress.com/wp-content/uploads/2020/01/scores.png?w=768 768w, https://chrisssims.wordpress.com/wp-content/uploads/2020/01/scores.png?w=1024 1024w, https://chrisssims.wordpress.com/wp-content/uploads/2020/01/scores.png 1344w" sizes="auto, (max-width: 810px) 100vw, 810px" data-attachment-id="27012" data-permalink="https://chrisssims.wordpress.com/2020/01/12/exceptional-scores/scores/" data-orig-file="https://chrisssims.wordpress.com/wp-content/uploads/2020/01/scores.png" data-orig-size="1344,528" data-comments-opened="1" data-image-meta="{&quot;aperture&quot;:&quot;0&quot;,&quot;credit&quot;:&quot;&quot;,&quot;camera&quot;:&quot;&quot;,&quot;caption&quot;:&quot;&quot;,&quot;created_timestamp&quot;:&quot;0&quot;,&quot;copyright&quot;:&quot;&quot;,&quot;focal_length&quot;:&quot;0&quot;,&quot;iso&quot;:&quot;0&quot;,&quot;shutter_speed&quot;:&quot;0&quot;,&quot;title&quot;:&quot;&quot;,&quot;orientation&quot;:&quot;0&quot;}" data-image-title="scores" data-image-description="&lt;p&gt;The Fall of the Rebel Angels by Pieter Bruegel the Elder (1562).&lt;/p&gt;
" data-image-caption="" data-large-file="https://chrisssims.wordpress.com/wp-content/uploads/2020/01/scores.png?w=809" />					<figcaption><p><i class="fa fa-file-text"></i></p></figcaption>
				</a>
			</figure>
		<header class="entry-header">
		<h1 class="entry-title"><a href="https://chrisssims.wordpress.com/2020/01/12/exceptional-scores/" rel="bookmark">Playing with Exceptional&nbsp;Scores</a></h1>					<div class="entry-meta small-part">
				<span class="posted-on"><i class="fa fa-clock-o space-left-right"></i><a href="https://chrisssims.wordpress.com/2020/01/12/exceptional-scores/" rel="bookmark"><time class="entry-date published" datetime="2020-01-12T18:27:22+01:00">January 12, 2020</time><time class="updated" datetime="2020-07-05T07:42:35+02:00">July 5, 2020</time></a></span><span class="byline"> <i class="fa fa-user space-left-right"></i><span class="author vcard"><a class="url fn n" href="https://chrisssims.wordpress.com/author/chrisssims/">Chris S. Sims</a></span></span><span class="comments-link"><i class="fa fa-comments-o space-left-right"></i><a href="https://chrisssims.wordpress.com/2020/01/12/exceptional-scores/#respond">Leave a comment</a></span>			</div><!-- .entry-meta -->
			</header><!-- .entry-header -->

			<div class="entry-content">
			<p>When it comes to a lot of D&amp;D-derived games <a href="#1">(1)</a>, ability scores have been a discussion for as long as the capabilities and bonuses they’ve given a character have been only derivative of those scores. Most of this design territory is an example of mechanics being too finicky for what they do but surviving nonetheless. The design at the time was functional and innovative, but that doesn’t render it good, originally or forever. These structures remain within the game largely due to legacy or nostalgia, not because they are still functional, innovative, or even necessary.</p>
<p>Some games moved the marker and, such as <a href="https://www.drivethrurpg.com/product/19360/True20-Adventure-Roleplaying?affiliate_id=931013" target="_blank" rel="noopener"><em>True20</em></a> did, answered the question, “If you need only a modifier, why isn’t that modifier the score?” Heck, <a href="https://www.drivethrurpg.com/product/16868/Players-Handbook-Revised-2e?affiliate_id=931013" target="_blank" rel="noopener">AD&amp;D’s second edition</a> made ability scores more useful, especially in the <a href="https://www.drivethrurpg.com/product/16863/Players-Option--Skills--Power-2e?affiliate_id=931013" target="_blank" rel="noopener"><em>Skills &amp; Powers</em></a> book. <a href="#2">(2)</a> These fiddly aspects merit such debate and reworking. It’s another aspect I’m interested in seeing jettisoned, and that’s the racial ability score adjustment, whatever a particular game calls it. Put another way, you are an orc, so you raise your Strength and Constitution scores by 2, and you lower your Intelligence by 2.<a class="more-link" href="https://chrisssims.wordpress.com/2020/01/12/exceptional-scores/">Read More &raquo;</a></p>
		</div><!-- .entry-content -->
	
	<footer class="entry-footer">
		<div class="entry-bottom small-part">
					</div>
	</footer><!-- .entry-footer -->
</article><!-- #post-## -->
			
				
<article id="post-26896" class="post-26896 post type-post status-publish format-standard has-post-thumbnail hentry category-advice category-game-design category-games category-graphic-design category-opinions category-roleplaying-games category-writing">
				<figure class="entry-featured-image">
				<a href="https://chrisssims.wordpress.com/2020/01/04/re-introductions/" rel="bookmark" title="Re Introductions">
					<img width="810" height="357" src="https://chrisssims.wordpress.com/wp-content/uploads/2020/01/eberron.png?w=810" class="attachment-nucleare-normal-post size-nucleare-normal-post wp-post-image" alt="by Brain “Chippy” Dugan" decoding="async" loading="lazy" srcset="https://chrisssims.wordpress.com/wp-content/uploads/2020/01/eberron.png?w=810 810w, https://chrisssims.wordpress.com/wp-content/uploads/2020/01/eberron.png?w=150 150w, https://chrisssims.wordpress.com/wp-content/uploads/2020/01/eberron.png?w=300 300w, https://chrisssims.wordpress.com/wp-content/uploads/2020/01/eberron.png?w=768 768w, https://chrisssims.wordpress.com/wp-content/uploads/2020/01/eberron.png?w=1024 1024w, https://chrisssims.wordpress.com/wp-content/uploads/2020/01/eberron.png 1131w" sizes="auto, (max-width: 810px) 100vw, 810px" data-attachment-id="26907" data-permalink="https://chrisssims.wordpress.com/2020/01/04/re-introductions/eberron/" data-orig-file="https://chrisssims.wordpress.com/wp-content/uploads/2020/01/eberron.png" data-orig-size="1131,499" data-comments-opened="1" data-image-meta="{&quot;aperture&quot;:&quot;0&quot;,&quot;credit&quot;:&quot;&quot;,&quot;camera&quot;:&quot;&quot;,&quot;caption&quot;:&quot;&quot;,&quot;created_timestamp&quot;:&quot;0&quot;,&quot;copyright&quot;:&quot;&quot;,&quot;focal_length&quot;:&quot;0&quot;,&quot;iso&quot;:&quot;0&quot;,&quot;shutter_speed&quot;:&quot;0&quot;,&quot;title&quot;:&quot;&quot;,&quot;orientation&quot;:&quot;0&quot;}" data-image-title="Eberron" data-image-description="" data-image-caption="&lt;p&gt;Art by Brain “Chippy” Dugan, from Eberron Campaign Guide and Eberron: Rising from the Last War&lt;/p&gt;
" data-large-file="https://chrisssims.wordpress.com/wp-content/uploads/2020/01/eberron.png?w=809" />					<figcaption><p><i class="fa fa-file-text"></i></p></figcaption>
				</a>
			</figure>
		<header class="entry-header">
		<h1 class="entry-title"><a href="https://chrisssims.wordpress.com/2020/01/04/re-introductions/" rel="bookmark">Re Introductions</a></h1>					<div class="entry-meta small-part">
				<span class="posted-on"><i class="fa fa-clock-o space-left-right"></i><a href="https://chrisssims.wordpress.com/2020/01/04/re-introductions/" rel="bookmark"><time class="entry-date published" datetime="2020-01-04T18:00:10+01:00">January 4, 2020</time><time class="updated" datetime="2020-01-23T15:31:50+01:00">January 23, 2020</time></a></span><span class="byline"> <i class="fa fa-user space-left-right"></i><span class="author vcard"><a class="url fn n" href="https://chrisssims.wordpress.com/author/chrisssims/">Chris S. Sims</a></span></span><span class="comments-link"><i class="fa fa-comments-o space-left-right"></i><a href="https://chrisssims.wordpress.com/2020/01/04/re-introductions/#comments">2 Comments</a></span>			</div><!-- .entry-meta -->
			</header><!-- .entry-header -->

			<div class="entry-content">
			<p>A couple weeks ago, I dove into opening sections to roleplaying game books and game setting books I own. I had thoughts. Such introductions are often lackluster, too much like a textbook and not enough fun. I rambled on about and engaged others on those thoughts in this Twitter thread (click the date in the quoted tweet).</p>
<blockquote><p>A good aspect of 4e campaign setting supplements, from Dark Sun to Underdark (although too understated there) was an aspect list that defined the setting in about a page. Glad to see it in the new Eberron. It&#8217;s a strong starting point and, perhaps, selling point.</p>
<p>— Chris S. Sims (@ChrisSSims) <a href="https://twitter.com/ChrisSSims/status/1207623778391461888" target="_blank" rel="noopener">December 19, 2019</a></p></blockquote>
<p><a class="more-link" href="https://chrisssims.wordpress.com/2020/01/04/re-introductions/">Read More &raquo;</a>		</p>
<div id="geo-post-26896" class="geo geo-post" style="display: none">
			<span class="latitude">47.698629</span><br />
			<span class="longitude">16.148824</span>
		</div>
		</div><!-- .entry-content -->
	
	<footer class="entry-footer">
