</article><!-- #post-## -->
			
				
<article id="post-26366" class="post-26366 post type-post status-publish format-standard has-post-thumbnail hentry category-game-design category-games category-opinions category-roleplaying category-roleplaying-games category-science-fiction-fantasy category-setting category-video-games category-world-building">
				<figure class="entry-featured-image">
				<a href="https://chrisssims.wordpress.com/2017/09/20/queer-creations/" rel="bookmark" title="World Building: Inclusivity">
					<img width="810" height="310" src="https://chrisssims.wordpress.com/wp-content/uploads/2017/09/love.png?w=810" class="attachment-nucleare-normal-post size-nucleare-normal-post wp-post-image" alt="" decoding="async" loading="lazy" srcset="https://chrisssims.wordpress.com/wp-content/uploads/2017/09/love.png?w=810 810w, https://chrisssims.wordpress.com/wp-content/uploads/2017/09/love.png?w=150 150w, https://chrisssims.wordpress.com/wp-content/uploads/2017/09/love.png?w=300 300w, https://chrisssims.wordpress.com/wp-content/uploads/2017/09/love.png?w=768 768w, https://chrisssims.wordpress.com/wp-content/uploads/2017/09/love.png?w=1024 1024w, https://chrisssims.wordpress.com/wp-content/uploads/2017/09/love.png 1222w" sizes="auto, (max-width: 810px) 100vw, 810px" data-attachment-id="26941" data-permalink="https://chrisssims.wordpress.com/2017/09/20/queer-creations/love/" data-orig-file="https://chrisssims.wordpress.com/wp-content/uploads/2017/09/love.png" data-orig-size="1222,468" data-comments-opened="1" data-image-meta="{&quot;aperture&quot;:&quot;0&quot;,&quot;credit&quot;:&quot;&quot;,&quot;camera&quot;:&quot;&quot;,&quot;caption&quot;:&quot;&quot;,&quot;created_timestamp&quot;:&quot;0&quot;,&quot;copyright&quot;:&quot;&quot;,&quot;focal_length&quot;:&quot;0&quot;,&quot;iso&quot;:&quot;0&quot;,&quot;shutter_speed&quot;:&quot;0&quot;,&quot;title&quot;:&quot;&quot;,&quot;orientation&quot;:&quot;0&quot;}" data-image-title="love" data-image-description="" data-image-caption="" data-large-file="https://chrisssims.wordpress.com/wp-content/uploads/2017/09/love.png?w=809" />					<figcaption><p><i class="fa fa-file-text"></i></p></figcaption>
				</a>
			</figure>
		<header class="entry-header">
		<h1 class="entry-title"><a href="https://chrisssims.wordpress.com/2017/09/20/queer-creations/" rel="bookmark">World Building: Inclusivity</a></h1>					<div class="entry-meta small-part">
				<span class="posted-on"><i class="fa fa-clock-o space-left-right"></i><a href="https://chrisssims.wordpress.com/2017/09/20/queer-creations/" rel="bookmark"><time class="entry-date published" datetime="2017-09-20T22:28:43+02:00">September 20, 2017</time><time class="updated" datetime="2020-01-23T12:40:28+01:00">January 23, 2020</time></a></span><span class="byline"> <i class="fa fa-user space-left-right"></i><span class="author vcard"><a class="url fn n" href="https://chrisssims.wordpress.com/author/chrisssims/">Chris S. Sims</a></span></span><span class="comments-link"><i class="fa fa-comments-o space-left-right"></i><a href="https://chrisssims.wordpress.com/2017/09/20/queer-creations/#respond">Leave a comment</a></span>			</div><!-- .entry-meta -->
			</header><!-- .entry-header -->

			<div class="entry-content">
			<p>Kotaku recently published an <a href="http://kotaku.com/dungeons-dragons-promises-to-make-the-game-more-queer-1798401117">article on queerness in the D&amp;D game</a>. To be more specific, this article is about the inclusion of queer people and, more specifically, a glimpse into their lives as normal, accepted citizens of imaginary worlds. The fifth edition <em>Player’s Handbook</em>, for the first time in D&amp;D history, makes a bold statement about sexuality and gender. It encourages you to imagine different. Several official D&amp;D adventures depict queer couples or families. Many other games have similar modes of presentation, nodding toward normalcy. All these steps are positive. However, a few failures of imagination exist with regard to depicting this sort of equality in games and other media. <a href="#1">(1)</a><a class="more-link" href="https://chrisssims.wordpress.com/2017/09/20/queer-creations/">Read More &raquo;</a></p>
		</div><!-- .entry-content -->
	
	<footer class="entry-footer">
		<div class="entry-bottom small-part">
					</div>
	</footer><!-- .entry-footer -->
</article><!-- #post-## -->
			
				
<article id="post-25867" class="post-25867 post type-post status-publish format-standard has-post-thumbnail hentry category-freelancing category-game-design category-game-mastering category-opinions category-roleplaying-games category-writing tag-dd tag-dungeons-and-dragons">
				<figure class="entry-featured-image">
				<a href="https://chrisssims.wordpress.com/2016/08/01/a-dd-life-2/" rel="bookmark" title="A D&amp;D Life">
					<img width="679" height="420" src="https://chrisssims.wordpress.com/wp-content/uploads/2016/08/expert-1.png?w=679" class="attachment-nucleare-normal-post size-nucleare-normal-post wp-post-image" alt="" decoding="async" loading="lazy" srcset="https://chrisssims.wordpress.com/wp-content/uploads/2016/08/expert-1.png 679w, https://chrisssims.wordpress.com/wp-content/uploads/2016/08/expert-1.png?w=150 150w, https://chrisssims.wordpress.com/wp-content/uploads/2016/08/expert-1.png?w=300 300w" sizes="auto, (max-width: 679px) 100vw, 679px" data-attachment-id="26996" data-permalink="https://chrisssims.wordpress.com/2016/08/01/a-dd-life-2/expert/" data-orig-file="https://chrisssims.wordpress.com/wp-content/uploads/2016/08/expert-1.png" data-orig-size="679,420" data-comments-opened="1" data-image-meta="{&quot;aperture&quot;:&quot;0&quot;,&quot;credit&quot;:&quot;&quot;,&quot;camera&quot;:&quot;&quot;,&quot;caption&quot;:&quot;&quot;,&quot;created_timestamp&quot;:&quot;0&quot;,&quot;copyright&quot;:&quot;&quot;,&quot;focal_length&quot;:&quot;0&quot;,&quot;iso&quot;:&quot;0&quot;,&quot;shutter_speed&quot;:&quot;0&quot;,&quot;title&quot;:&quot;&quot;,&quot;orientation&quot;:&quot;0&quot;}" data-image-title="expert" data-image-description="" data-image-caption="" data-large-file="https://chrisssims.wordpress.com/wp-content/uploads/2016/08/expert-1.png?w=679" />					<figcaption><p><i class="fa fa-file-text"></i></p></figcaption>
				</a>
			</figure>
		<header class="entry-header">
		<h1 class="entry-title"><a href="https://chrisssims.wordpress.com/2016/08/01/a-dd-life-2/" rel="bookmark">A D&amp;D Life</a></h1>					<div class="entry-meta small-part">
				<span class="posted-on"><i class="fa fa-clock-o space-left-right"></i><a href="https://chrisssims.wordpress.com/2016/08/01/a-dd-life-2/" rel="bookmark"><time class="entry-date published" datetime="2016-08-01T08:30:02+02:00">August 1, 2016</time><time class="updated" datetime="2020-01-23T16:11:21+01:00">January 23, 2020</time></a></span><span class="byline"> <i class="fa fa-user space-left-right"></i><span class="author vcard"><a class="url fn n" href="https://chrisssims.wordpress.com/author/chrisssims/">Chris S. Sims</a></span></span><span class="comments-link"><i class="fa fa-comments-o space-left-right"></i><a href="https://chrisssims.wordpress.com/2016/08/01/a-dd-life-2/#respond">Leave a comment</a></span>			</div><!-- .entry-meta -->
			</header><!-- .entry-header -->

			<div class="entry-content">
			<p><figure data-shortcode="caption" id="attachment_26967" aria-describedby="caption-attachment-26967" style="width: 234px" class="wp-caption alignleft"><img data-attachment-id="26967" data-permalink="https://chrisssims.wordpress.com/2016/08/01/a-dd-life-2/basic/" data-orig-file="https://chrisssims.wordpress.com/wp-content/uploads/2016/08/basic.png" data-orig-size="234,300" data-comments-opened="1" data-image-meta="{&quot;aperture&quot;:&quot;0&quot;,&quot;credit&quot;:&quot;&quot;,&quot;camera&quot;:&quot;&quot;,&quot;caption&quot;:&quot;&quot;,&quot;created_timestamp&quot;:&quot;0&quot;,&quot;copyright&quot;:&quot;&quot;,&quot;focal_length&quot;:&quot;0&quot;,&quot;iso&quot;:&quot;0&quot;,&quot;shutter_speed&quot;:&quot;0&quot;,&quot;title&quot;:&quot;&quot;,&quot;orientation&quot;:&quot;0&quot;}" data-image-title="Basic" data-image-description="" data-image-caption="&lt;p&gt;My first magic tome.&lt;/p&gt;
" data-large-file="https://chrisssims.wordpress.com/wp-content/uploads/2016/08/basic.png?w=234" loading="lazy" class="alignnone size-full wp-image-26967" src="https://chrisssims.wordpress.com/wp-content/uploads/2016/08/basic.png" alt="Basic" width="234" height="300" srcset="https://chrisssims.wordpress.com/wp-content/uploads/2016/08/basic.png 234w, https://chrisssims.wordpress.com/wp-content/uploads/2016/08/basic.png?w=117&amp;h=150 117w" sizes="auto, (max-width: 234px) 100vw, 234px" /><figcaption id="caption-attachment-26967" class="wp-caption-text">My first magic tome</figcaption></figure></p>
<p>What does D&amp;D mean to me? My friend Shawn Merwin asked me to write about this question, and record the response for his podcast. I don&#8217;t have recording gear (or skills), so I wrote this piece. He recorded it for his podcast.</p>
<p>The question itself brings up all sorts of feelings and memories. It&#8217;s an important question, because some might think after being laid off (twice) while working on D&amp;D, I might have negative feelings about it. I don&#8217;t. From the heady days of first gaming in 1981 to today, working on three or four different game projects at once, D&amp;D has been and is still good to me.<a class="more-link" href="https://chrisssims.wordpress.com/2016/08/01/a-dd-life-2/">Read More &raquo;</a></p>
		</div><!-- .entry-content -->
	
	<footer class="entry-footer">
		<div class="entry-bottom small-part">
					</div>
	</footer><!-- .entry-footer -->
</article><!-- #post-## -->
			
				
<article id="post-25752" class="post-25752 post type-post status-publish format-standard has-post-thumbnail hentry category-advice category-game-design category-game-mastering category-roleplaying-games category-science-fiction-fantasy category-setting category-world-building category-writing tag-dd tag-dm tag-dungeon-mastering tag-dungeons-and-dragons tag-game-mastering tag-gm tag-roleplaying tag-world-building tag-world-design tag-worldbuilding">
				<figure class="entry-featured-image">
				<a href="https://chrisssims.wordpress.com/2016/06/02/world-building-roots-2/" rel="bookmark" title="World Building: Roots">
					<img width="810" height="257" src="https://chrisssims.wordpress.com/wp-content/uploads/2016/06/roots_of_big_old_tree-1.png?w=810" class="attachment-nucleare-normal-post size-nucleare-normal-post wp-post-image" alt="" decoding="async" loading="lazy" srcset="https://chrisssims.wordpress.com/wp-content/uploads/2016/06/roots_of_big_old_tree-1.png?w=810 810w, https://chrisssims.wordpress.com/wp-content/uploads/2016/06/roots_of_big_old_tree-1.png?w=150 150w, https://chrisssims.wordpress.com/wp-content/uploads/2016/06/roots_of_big_old_tree-1.png?w=300 300w, https://chrisssims.wordpress.com/wp-content/uploads/2016/06/roots_of_big_old_tree-1.png?w=768 768w, https://chrisssims.wordpress.com/wp-content/uploads/2016/06/roots_of_big_old_tree-1.png?w=1024 1024w, https://chrisssims.wordpress.com/wp-content/uploads/2016/06/roots_of_big_old_tree-1.png 1212w" sizes="auto, (max-width: 810px) 100vw, 810px" data-attachment-id="26955" data-permalink="https://chrisssims.wordpress.com/2016/06/02/world-building-roots-2/roots_of_big_old_tree/" data-orig-file="https://chrisssims.wordpress.com/wp-content/uploads/2016/06/roots_of_big_old_tree-1.png" data-orig-size="1212,384" data-comments-opened="1" data-image-meta="{&quot;aperture&quot;:&quot;0&quot;,&quot;credit&quot;:&quot;&quot;,&quot;camera&quot;:&quot;&quot;,&quot;caption&quot;:&quot;&quot;,&quot;created_timestamp&quot;:&quot;0&quot;,&quot;copyright&quot;:&quot;&quot;,&quot;focal_length&quot;:&quot;0&quot;,&quot;iso&quot;:&quot;0&quot;,&quot;shutter_speed&quot;:&quot;0&quot;,&quot;title&quot;:&quot;&quot;,&quot;orientation&quot;:&quot;0&quot;}" data-image-title="Roots_of_big_old_tree" data-image-description="" data-image-caption="" data-large-file="https://chrisssims.wordpress.com/wp-content/uploads/2016/06/roots_of_big_old_tree-1.png?w=809" />					<figcaption><p><i class="fa fa-file-text"></i></p></figcaption>
				</a>
			</figure>
		<header class="entry-header">
		<h1 class="entry-title"><a href="https://chrisssims.wordpress.com/2016/06/02/world-building-roots-2/" rel="bookmark">World Building: Roots</a></h1>					<div class="entry-meta small-part">
				<span class="posted-on"><i class="fa fa-clock-o space-left-right"></i><a href="https://chrisssims.wordpress.com/2016/06/02/world-building-roots-2/" rel="bookmark"><time class="entry-date published" datetime="2016-06-02T08:30:11+02:00">June 2, 2016</time><time class="updated" datetime="2020-01-21T12:02:41+01:00">January 21, 2020</time></a></span><span class="byline"> <i class="fa fa-user space-left-right"></i><span class="author vcard"><a class="url fn n" href="https://chrisssims.wordpress.com/author/chrisssims/">Chris S. Sims</a></span></span><span class="comments-link"><i class="fa fa-comments-o space-left-right"></i><a href="https://chrisssims.wordpress.com/2016/06/02/world-building-roots-2/#respond">Leave a comment</a></span>			</div><!-- .entry-meta -->
			</header><!-- .entry-header -->

			<div class="entry-content">
			<p><figure data-shortcode="caption" id="attachment_26956" aria-describedby="caption-attachment-26956" style="width: 300px" class="wp-caption alignright"><img data-attachment-id="26956" data-permalink="https://chrisssims.wordpress.com/2016/06/02/world-building-roots-2/marshubble/" data-orig-file="https://chrisssims.wordpress.com/wp-content/uploads/2016/06/marshubble.jpg" data-orig-size="300,272" data-comments-opened="1" data-image-meta="{&quot;aperture&quot;:&quot;0&quot;,&quot;credit&quot;:&quot;&quot;,&quot;camera&quot;:&quot;&quot;,&quot;caption&quot;:&quot;&quot;,&quot;created_timestamp&quot;:&quot;0&quot;,&quot;copyright&quot;:&quot;&quot;,&quot;focal_length&quot;:&quot;0&quot;,&quot;iso&quot;:&quot;0&quot;,&quot;shutter_speed&quot;:&quot;0&quot;,&quot;title&quot;:&quot;&quot;,&quot;orientation&quot;:&quot;0&quot;}" data-image-title="marshubble" data-image-description="" data-image-caption="" data-large-file="https://chrisssims.wordpress.com/wp-content/uploads/2016/06/marshubble.jpg?w=300" loading="lazy" class=" size-full wp-image-26956 alignright" src="https://chrisssims.wordpress.com/wp-content/uploads/2016/06/marshubble.jpg" alt="marshubble" width="300" height="272" srcset="https://chrisssims.wordpress.com/wp-content/uploads/2016/06/marshubble.jpg 300w, https://chrisssims.wordpress.com/wp-content/uploads/2016/06/marshubble.jpg?w=150&amp;h=136 150w" sizes="auto, (max-width: 300px) 100vw, 300px" /><figcaption id="caption-attachment-26956" class="wp-caption-text">Barsoom (2)</figcaption></figure></p>
<p style="text-align:left;">I said a while ago that I wanted to talk about world building (maybe <em>worldbuilding</em> or<em> world-building</em>, as you prefer). That I do. Doing so seems likely to take more than a couple entries here. This essay is the beginning, written as much for me to explore what I know as for anyone who cares enough to read it. (1)</p>
<p>Generation of the world or universe, the setting, is important to numerous aspects of creating media, from novels to games. Careful design can&#8217;t be undervalued. Assumptions should be avoided, while reasoned relationships should take prominence. Aim to build novelty and interest, but include enough of the familiar to build resonance with the audience.<a class="more-link" href="https://chrisssims.wordpress.com/2016/06/02/world-building-roots-2/">Read More &raquo;</a></p>
		</div><!-- .entry-content -->
	
	<footer class="entry-footer">
		<div class="entry-bottom small-part">
					</div>
	</footer><!-- .entry-footer -->
</article><!-- #post-## -->
			
